settings-transitions-transitions-card = Transitions
settings-transitions-transitions-card-desc = Choose how one wallpaper changes into the next. The same settings apply to images, videos, and Wallpaper Engine scenes.
settings-transitions-enable-label = Enable transitions
settings-transitions-enable-desc = Off cuts straight to the new wallpaper.
settings-transitions-duration-label = Duration
settings-transitions-duration-desc = Set the total transition time in milliseconds. Sand transitions need at least 4000 ms for the grain movement to remain visible.
settings-transitions-family-label = Family
settings-transitions-shader-label = Transition
settings-transitions-shader-count-desc = { $count } in this family.
settings-transitions-preview-card = Preview
settings-transitions-preview-card-desc = Loop the selected transition using the duration and performance settings below.
settings-transitions-show-preview-label = Show preview
settings-transitions-show-preview-desc = Run the transition renderer while this tab is open. Turn it off to stop its CPU and GPU use.
settings-transitions-preview-fps-label = Preview frame rate
settings-transitions-preview-fps-desc = The whole picker repaints every preview frame. 30 is smooth; 120 spends about four times the CPU for no visible gain. Capped at Max FPS.
settings-transitions-sand-card = Transition performance
settings-transitions-sand-card-desc = Choose whether each transition runs on every monitor or only the primary monitor. The global switch above is the only Off control.
settings-transitions-quality-label = Quality
settings-transitions-quality-desc = Auto runs full resolution at 60 fps on discrete GPUs and Low on integrated. Full is uncapped; Low caps at 30 fps at reduced resolution, about 4.5x cheaper.
settings-transitions-quality-auto = Auto
settings-transitions-quality-full = Full
settings-transitions-quality-low = Low
settings-transitions-scope-desc = All animates this shader on every updated monitor. Primary animates it once and changes the other monitors immediately.
settings-transitions-scope-all = All monitors
settings-transitions-scope-primary = Primary only
settings-transitions-primary-label = Primary monitor
settings-transitions-primary-desc = Output that animates when a shader is set to Primary, e.g. DP-2. Empty uses the first available output.
settings-transitions-sharp-label = Sharpen reduced sand
settings-transitions-sharp-desc = FSR1-style sharpen on the lower-resolution sand. Slightly more GPU; only active while quality reduces resolution.
settings-transitions-family-random = Random
settings-transitions-family-random-desc = A different transition every time.
settings-transitions-family-fade = Fade
settings-transitions-family-fade-desc = Dissolves and blends, no geometry.
settings-transitions-family-wipe = Wipe
settings-transitions-family-wipe-desc = A shape or edge sweeps across the screen.
settings-transitions-family-warp = Warp
settings-transitions-family-warp-desc = The image bends, stretches or ripples.
settings-transitions-family-break = Break up
settings-transitions-family-break-desc = The image shatters, pixelates or smears.
settings-transitions-family-sand = Sand
settings-transitions-family-sand-desc = Every pixel becomes a grain and flies into a shape.

settings-transitions-rate-label = Transition FPS
settings-transitions-rate-desc = Limit animation frames per second without changing wallpaper playback. Leave empty or enter 0 for each display's refresh rate.
settings-transitions-rate-auto = Auto

settings-drawing-card = Drawing transitions
settings-drawing-card-desc = Prepare an image, video or supported Wallpaper Engine wallpaper for Drawing. Processing runs once, before playback; cached drawings play without the processing files.
settings-drawing-enable-label = Draw prepared wallpapers by default
settings-drawing-enable-desc = Use Drawing for prepared wallpapers without a card choice. Draw or Drawn on a card overrides this default. Ordinary transitions are independent.
settings-drawing-enable-unprepared = Prepare the selected wallpaper before enabling Drawing transitions.
settings-drawing-paper-label = Paper colour
settings-drawing-paper-desc = The background the drawing is made on.
settings-drawing-ink-label = Ink colour
settings-drawing-ink-desc = The colour of the drawn lines.
settings-drawing-ink-style-label = Ink
settings-drawing-ink-style-desc = Plain lines use the ink colour. Rainbow lines run through the spectrum.
settings-drawing-ink-style-plain = Plain
settings-drawing-ink-style-rainbow = Rainbow
settings-drawing-duration-label = Duration
settings-drawing-duration-desc = Total time for the drawing and finish in milliseconds, from 1500 to 20000.
settings-drawing-battery-label = Prepare on battery power
settings-drawing-battery-desc = Allow processing while unplugged. When off, preparation pauses on battery; prepared drawings can still play.
settings-drawing-library-label = Prepare all wallpapers
settings-drawing-library-desc = Prepare every wallpaper that has Drawing on, including videos and Wallpaper Engine. Prepared wallpapers are skipped, so a stopped run continues where it left off.
settings-drawing-library-action = Prepare all
settings-drawing-library-stop = Stop
settings-drawing-library-skipped = { $count } skipped
settings-drawing-auto-label = Prepare new wallpapers automatically
settings-drawing-auto-desc = After each library scan, prepare wallpapers with Drawing on that are not prepared yet. Pausing holds this until you resume; stopping turns it off.
settings-drawing-pack-label = Processing files
settings-drawing-pack-missing = No processing files are registered. Choose a local Drawing pack manifest to prepare wallpapers.
settings-drawing-pack-checking = Checking the processing files and runtime. You can cancel this check.
settings-drawing-pack-install = Install the skwd-drawing-model package to use Drawing.
settings-drawing-pack-ready = Processing files are available. They are used only while preparing a wallpaper.
settings-drawing-pack-invalid = The registered processing files could not be used. Choose a valid Drawing pack manifest.
settings-drawing-pack-action-label = Choose processing files
settings-drawing-pack-action-desc = Select the manifest from a locally installed Drawing processing pack. This does not download files.
settings-drawing-pack-action = Choose manifest
settings-drawing-pack-picker-title = Choose Drawing pack manifest
settings-drawing-pack-picker-filter = JSON manifest | *.json
settings-drawing-detach-label = Detach processing files
settings-drawing-detach-desc = Stop using the registered processing pack. Prepared drawings remain cached and playable.
settings-drawing-detach-action = Detach files
settings-drawing-selection-label = Selected wallpaper
settings-drawing-selection-none = Select a wallpaper
settings-drawing-selection-unprepared = This wallpaper is not prepared. It uses the ordinary transition setting; when that is off, the wallpaper changes immediately.
settings-drawing-selection-prepared = Prepared. The drawing can play without the processing files.
settings-drawing-selection-checking = Checking the processing files before preparation.
settings-drawing-selection-preparing = Preparing the selected wallpaper.
settings-drawing-selection-cancelled = Preparation was cancelled. The wallpaper can be prepared again.
settings-drawing-selection-failed = Preparation failed. See the error and try again.
settings-drawing-checking-label = Checking processing files
settings-drawing-checking-desc = Validating the local pack and its runtime. This may take a moment.
settings-drawing-progress-label = Preparation
settings-drawing-progress-value = { $stage } · { $percent }% · { $completed }/{ $total } done
settings-drawing-prepare-desc = Prepare the selected wallpaper for Drawing. Videos and Wallpaper Engine scenes use a captured frame.
settings-drawing-prepare-action = Prepare selected wallpaper
settings-drawing-prepare-again-action = Prepare again
settings-drawing-cancel-desc = Stop preparation. Finished cached drawings are kept.
settings-drawing-cancel-action = Cancel preparation
settings-drawing-preview-desc = Play this drawing on the desktop using the selected colours and duration. The picker hides so you can see it; use the Wall shortcut to return. This does not enable Drawing transitions.
settings-drawing-preview-action = Preview on desktop
settings-drawing-cache-label = Drawing cache
settings-drawing-clear-desc = Delete prepared drawings from the cache. Processing files stay registered.
settings-drawing-clear-action = Clear Drawing cache
settings-drawing-unavailable-label = Drawing is unavailable
settings-drawing-unavailable-desc = Register processing files to prepare new wallpapers, or use an already prepared wallpaper.
settings-drawing-error = Drawing failed: { $error }
settings-drawing-selection-paused = Preparation is paused. Cached drawings remain available.
settings-drawing-pause-desc = Stop processing and release the models. Resume starts preparation again for this wallpaper.
settings-drawing-pause-action = Pause preparation
settings-drawing-resume-desc = Start preparing the selected wallpaper again. Completed cached drawings remain available.
settings-drawing-resume-action = Resume preparation
settings-drawing-pack-size = Model files: { $size }
settings-drawing-stage-checking = Checking wallpaper
settings-drawing-stage-ready = Ready to prepare
settings-drawing-stage-starting = Starting models
settings-drawing-stage-source = Reading source image
settings-drawing-stage-lineart = Finding lines
settings-drawing-stage-depth = Mapping depth
settings-drawing-stage-subjects = Finding subjects
settings-drawing-stage-complete = Drawing ready
settings-drawing-stage-other = Preparing image
settings-drawing-selection-other-preparing = Another wallpaper is being prepared. Pause or cancel it before preparing this one.
settings-drawing-selection-other-paused = Another wallpaper is paused. Resume or cancel it before preparing this one.
settings-drawing-scope-label = Prepare
settings-drawing-scope-desc = Choose one wallpaper or the current filtered view. Images, videos and supported Wallpaper Engine wallpapers can be prepared, up to 128 at a time.
settings-drawing-scope-selected = Selected wallpaper
settings-drawing-scope-view = Current view
settings-drawing-view-count-label = Wallpapers in current view
settings-drawing-view-count = { $count } wallpapers in the current filtered view.
settings-drawing-view-empty-label = No wallpapers in this view
settings-drawing-view-empty-desc = Change the current filter or choose a wallpaper before preparing this view.
settings-drawing-view-limit-label = Too many wallpapers
settings-drawing-view-limit-desc = This view has { $count } wallpapers. Narrow the filter to { $limit } or fewer before preparing it.
settings-drawing-prepare-view-desc = Prepare the wallpapers in the current filtered view, one at a time. Existing cached drawings are kept.
settings-drawing-prepare-view-action = Prepare { $count } wallpapers
settings-drawing-selection-view-preparing = Preparing the current view. Only cached wallpapers will use Drawing transitions.
settings-drawing-selection-view-paused = Preparation of the current view is paused. Resume or cancel it below.

settings-transitions-family-studio = Studio
settings-transitions-family-studio-desc = Cut, folded and staged transitions.
settings-transitions-preset-timing-label = Use preset timing
settings-transitions-preset-timing-desc = Use the timing designed for this transition: { $duration } ms. Turn off to set a custom duration.
settings-transitions-effect-photo-cutout = Photo cutout
settings-transitions-effect-slat-turn = Spinning photo slats
settings-transitions-effect-crop-relay = Crop relay
settings-transitions-effect-sunlit-arcade = Sunlit arcade
settings-transitions-effect-paper-heart = Framed paper heart
settings-drawing-device-label = Preparation device
settings-drawing-device-desc = Choose what runs the models while a wallpaper is prepared. Automatic uses the Drawing pack's own choice, which tries CUDA, then WebGPU, then the CPU. Only Automatic retries on the CPU when a run goes over the memory limit. The CPU works on every machine but is the slowest.
settings-drawing-device-auto = Automatic
settings-drawing-device-cuda = CUDA (NVIDIA)
settings-drawing-device-webgpu = WebGPU
settings-drawing-device-cpu = CPU
settings-drawing-memory-label = Memory limit
settings-drawing-memory-desc = The most memory preparation can use before it is stopped. Automatic keeps the standard 6 GiB limit. Raise it if large wallpapers fail to prepare, or lower it to leave more memory for other apps. With the Automatic device, a GPU run that goes over the limit is retried on the CPU.
settings-drawing-memory-auto = Automatic (6 GiB)
settings-drawing-memory-gib = { $gib } GiB
settings-drawing-memory-mib = { $mib } MiB
